From 004f551653c4b9deac81cb89e95c905beea637c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:17:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: decode mimic without direct rendering

MIMIC, MSN Messenger's webcam codec, predicts a picture from any of the 16
before it and keeps them all. With direct rendering, they were pictures of
the output's pool, sized for a few pictures held by a decoder: the pool
ran out a few pictures into the stream, and the decoder waited for a
picture none would free while the clock ran on. Decode MIMIC into the
decoder's own buffers, copied into the output's pictures, as the codecs
already left out of direct rendering are.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/video.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
index b8a3dca..802f613 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
@@ -542,7 +542,11 @@ static int InitVideoDecCommon( decoder_t *p_dec )
         /* No idea why ... but this fixes flickering on some TSCC streams */
         p_sys->p_codec->id != AV_CODEC_ID_TSCC &&
         p_sys->p_codec->id != AV_CODEC_ID_CSCD &&
-        p_sys->p_codec->id != AV_CODEC_ID_CINEPAK )
+        p_sys->p_codec->id != AV_CODEC_ID_CINEPAK &&
+        /* MIMIC keeps the last 16 pictures to predict from: drawn into the
+         * output's pictures, they held the pool, and the decoder waited for
+         * a picture none would free, a few pictures into the stream. */
+        p_sys->p_codec->id != AV_CODEC_ID_MIMIC )
     {
         /* Some codecs set pix_fmt only after the 1st frame has been decoded,
          * so we need to do another check in ffmpeg_GetFrameBuf() */
